>> title: Falafel
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: chickpeas, middle eastern, deep-fry, herbs, vegan
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: falafel, felafel, falafil, falaafil, ta'ameya, taameya, tameya, chickpea fritters, herb fritters
>> pairs-with: tahini-sauce, pita-bread, kabis
>> servings: 6
>> time: 25 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — the chickpeas are soaked and never cooked; a cooked one has nothing left to bind and falls apart in the oil or fries to a brick
>> step.1: soak the dried chickpeas 24 hr — never cook them
>> step.2: grind coarse with the herbs and aromatics
>> step.3: chill the mix 1 hr
>> step.4: work in the baking powder, shape
>> step.5: fry at 350°F 3 min

Cover @dried chickpeas{2%cups}(400 g) with cold water by four inches and ~soak{24%hr}, changing the water once.

Grind @&(~1)soaked chickpeas{}(drained and patted dry) with @flat-leaf parsley{1%cup}(packed), @cilantro{1%cup}(packed), @yellow onion{1%small}(quartered), @garlic{4%cloves}, @ground cumin{1%Tbs}, @ground coriander{2%tsp}, @cayenne{1/2%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp} and @black pepper{1%tsp} in a #food processor{} in three batches, pulsing to the texture of coarse wet sand.

Chill @&(~1)falafel mix{} covered ~chill{1%hr}.

Work @baking powder{1%tsp}(4 g) and @sesame seeds{2%Tbs} through @&(~1)chilled mix{} and shape it into flattened balls the size of a walnut, packing each one firmly between your palms.

Fry @&(~1)shaped falafel{} in @neutral oil{6%cups}(1.4 L; at 350°F/175°C) six at a time ~fry{3%min}, turning once, until they are deep brown and float high.
